cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use openproceedings in a systematic review or other research, please cite it as below, and report
  the index_version your searches ran on (each search record and export names it) so others can reproduce
  them.
type: software
title: "openproceedings: exact, reproducible Boolean search over NeurIPS, ICLR and ICML titles and abstracts"
abstract: >-
  openproceedings is exact, reproducible Boolean search over the titles and abstracts of NeurIPS, ICLR and
  ICML papers, built for systematic reviews. A query matches only on exact normalized tokens (no stemming or
  synonyms), filters live in the query string, default track and status filters report how many records they
  exclude, and every result set is pinned to an immutable index_version, so a saved search record replays to
  the same ids. Exports (RIS, CSV, BibTeX, JSONL) name each abstract's source.
authors:
  - given-names: Jeevan
    family-names: Parmar
    affiliation: "SHARE Lab, University of Waterloo"
  - name: "PLACEHOLDER: remaining authors to be confirmed"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uw-share-lab/openproceedings"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - boolean search
  - information retrieval
  - reproducibility
  - NeurIPS
  - ICLR
  - ICML
